  message: "Done in PR #2291 (dev 703dce32b; commits 34a08311d, cf35f03ff; Dart parts via WI-doboh/WI-kovok fixes 82e4bdff1, 0ba139f47). Live on dev 703dce32b: python ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/closure_pr3/sig_repros.py tojov -> 'ALL OK (15/15)': Java/Groovy (Foo.Bar x) vs (Baz.Bar x) hash '(Foo.Bar)' / '(Baz.Bar)' (distinct); Swift (x: Int.Type) -> '(Int.Type)' vs String.Type distinct; Swift tuple (Int, A.B) vs (Int, C.D) distinct; Swift/Kotlin function types keep their parameters ('((Int) -> B)' vs '((String) -> B)'); Kotlin suspend, receiver function type (StringBuilder.() -> Unit vs () -> Unit), annotated @Ann a.B vs a.C distinct; C# 'ref Foo.Bar' vs 'ref Foo.Baz' and '((int, A.B)?)' vs '((int, A.C)?)' distinct; Scala Int => a.B vs Long => a.B and Chain.NonEmpty vs Other.NonEmpty distinct; Rust (self, x: i32) -> '(Self,i32)' vs (&mut self, x: i32) -> '(&mut Self,i32)'. split_params_top_level keeps 'a: ((Int) -> Int, (Int) -> Int)', 'a: Map<(Int) -> Int, String>', 'x: {a: A, b: B}', Go 'x struct{a, b int}' and 'x interface{ M(a, b int) }' each whole, and 's: String = \")\"' whole; find_matching_paren('(a: String = \")\", b: Int) -> X', 0) = 24, the real closer. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/closure_pr3/tojov.txt"  # 73e9
